  "text_md": "Selecting  the  cent  as  the  denomination  (in order  to  avoid  fractions)  we express the  statement II  in  algebraic  symbols. .\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nCheck. 6  dimes  =60 cents, 5  half  dollars =  250  cents,  their  sum is -  $3.10.\n\n## EXERCISE\n\n## 38\n\n1. Two  numbers  differ  by 53, and  the  greater  is  four  times\n2. the  smaller. Find  the  numbers.\n2. Find  two  numbers  whose sum is  72-and the  greater which  equals  five  times  the  smaller.\n4. of\n3. The  difference between two  numbers  is  8, and  if  16  be added  to  the  greater,  the  result  will  be three  times  the  smaller. Find  the  numbers.  -\n4. The difference between two  numbers is  2, and  the  dif-\n7. ference  between  their  squares  is 16. Find  the  numbers.\n5. The  sum  of two  numbers is  47,  and  their  difference  is 9.\n9. Find  the  numbers.\n6. Divide 20  into  two  parts,  one  of  which  increased by 14\n11. shall  be  equal  to  the  other  increased  by 10.\n7. One  number  is 5 less  than  three times  another  number. If  the  second number is  subtracted from five  times the  first number,  the  result  is 25. What  are  the  numbers  ?\n8. Divide  22  into  two  parts  such  that  one  part  multiplied\n14. by 5 is equal  to  the  other  part  diminished  by 2.\n9. Find  two  consecutive numbers whose sum  is  equal  to\n243. |",
